is row `k` of the paper's table (`paper/v6/rare-discussion.tex`, paragraph A
noninterval optimal assignment). Its claimed interval has endpoints
`(lo_k+10⁻⁷)/1024` and `(hi_k-10⁻⁷)/1024`, strictly inside the paper's open interval
`(lo_k,hi_k)` scaled by `h = 1/1024`. The evidence trees are untrusted rational
data, accepted only by the checker `DeterministicCertificates.check` through
`accepted_sound`. Logarithms use the atanh series with ten terms and Mathlib's
geometric remainder (`unitLog`), square roots are checked by squaring, and every
intermediate interval is rounded outward to the grid `2⁻⁶⁴`. The scratch generator
that produced the trees is not part of the trusted base. -/
